  "paragraph": "Global equities were mixed in the latest completed round of trading, with 13 of the 24 benchmarks tracked on this page closing higher. In the United States, the S&P 500 was little changed at 7,704.13, the Dow Jones fell 0.31 per cent to 51,350, the Nasdaq Composite was little changed at 26,939 and the Russell 2000 fell 0.11 per cent to 2,835.57. In Europe, the FTSE 100 rose 0.54 per cent to 10,738, the DAX rose 0.91 per cent to 25,497 and the CAC 40 rose 0.37 per cent to 8,111.18. Across Asia, the Nikkei 225 rose 1.30 per cent to 66,364, the Hang Seng fell 1.01 per cent to 24,510, the KOSPI rose 1.04 per cent to 7,080.92, the Shanghai Composite fell 1.22 per cent to 3,888.37, the BSE Sensex rose 0.37 per cent to 73,850 and the Straits Times rose 0.48 per cent to 5,710.65. Elsewhere, the Ibovespa fell 0.99 per cent to 183,966. Locally, the S&P/ASX 200 fell 0.43 per cent to 8,665.00 and the All Ordinaries fell 0.58 per cent to 8,845.60. In digital assets, bitcoin changed hands at $84,741, up 2.03 per cent over the past 24 hours. In currencies, the US dollar bought 1.4232 Australian dollars, up 0.58 per cent against the prior business day's fix. Index levels, exchange rates and commodity prices on this page are captured live at build time from the sources linked in each section; no forward-looking view is offered here.",
